6.2.8.8 Events
The runtime also provides a way to closely monitor the device’s progress, as well as perform accurate
timing, by letting the application asynchronously recordevents at any point in the program, and query
when these events are completed. 
An event has completed when all tasks - or optionally, all commands
in a given stream - preceding the event have completed. 
Events in stream zero are completed after all
preceding tasks and commands in all streams are completed. 
